    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15909" root="رعظ" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَعِظٌ</span></b>  An arrow <i>having its</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُعْظ</span> <i>broken:</i> (S:)
and [in like manner,] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرعُوظٌ</span></b>  an arrow <i>having
its</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُعْظ</span> <i>broken, and being therefore bound with
sinew:</i> (IB:) or the latter signifies a <i>weak</i> arrow.
(Aboo-Kheyreh El-'Adawee, Ibn-' Abbád.)

